---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout 
  title="Terms — Cutline" 
  description="What Cutline is and is not. A public disclaimer for the Narge hostname list feed."
>
  <h1>Terms</h1>

  <section class="intro">
    <p class="lead">
      This is a plain-language notice about what Cutline is and what it is not. 
      It is not a terms of service. You are not signing a contract.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What Cutline Is</h2>
    <p>
      Cutline is an open-source hostname list feed. It is maintained by Dov Allison as a free public service.
    </p>
    <p>
      The purpose of Cutline is to provide a subscribeable list of hostnames classified under the 
      <a href="/spec">Narge content class</a>. Organizations can load this list into their own DNS servers 
      or firewalls. That is the only purpose. If you do not want the Narge content class to resolve on a 
      device or network, you may load the Cutline feed into your infrastructure.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What Cutline Is Not</h2>
    <p>
      Cutline is not a business. It is not a product for sale. It is not a warranty. It is not a kids safety service, 
      a compliance service, or a comprehensive solution beyond the narrow Narge class.
    </p>
    <p>
      There is no company. There is no signup. There is no charge.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Use at Your Own Risk</h2>
    <p>
      You choose to load this list into your infrastructure. You are responsible for that choice.
    </p>
    <p>
      We do not promise that every Narge name is on the list. We do not promise that every non-Narge name stays up. 
      The list is an approximation. This is an extra tool, not a guarantee.
    </p>
    <p>
      We are not responsible for what you can or cannot reach. We are not responsible for other software on your devices. 
      We are not responsible for anyone else's use of the same list.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Privacy</h2>
    <p>
      The hosted feed at <code>https://feeds.thecutline.org</code> counts usage without storing addresses. 
      Addresses are dropped at once; only distinct fetching addresses per ASN per day are counted. Aggregated stats 
      are published only when ≥10 distinct addresses in that ASN that day. For more detail, see the 
      <a href="/privacy-design">Privacy Design</a> and <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      The GitHub mirror has no measurement.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Open Source</h2>
    <p>
      The feed infrastructure, block list sources, and overlay corrections are all public. You can read exactly what is 
      happening and verify it yourself. See the <a href="/spec">Narge specification</a> and the 
      <a href="https://github.com/dov-max/narge-spec" target="_blank" rel="noopener">narge-spec repository</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Feedback</h2>
    <p>
      If you have questions, found a problem, or want to propose a change to the host list, open an issue on 
      <a href="https://github.com/dov-max/narge-spec/issues" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Not Legal Advice</h2>
    <p>
      This page is a notice. It describes what Cutline is and what it is not. It is not legal advice. 
      It does not create rights or obligations beyond what the law already provides.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .intro {
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-xl);
  }

  .lead {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  section {
    margin: var(--spacing-2xl) 0;
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
  }

  p {
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
</style>
